See-through (https://github.com/shitagaki-lab/see-through, Apache-2.0) at
commit df019de, changed to run on an Apple GPU (MPS). Apply in its folder:
  git checkout df019de && git apply <skill>/rigkit/vendor/see-through-mac.patch
- the device is cuda, mps or cpu, whichever there is (it was cuda only);
- the models load in bf16 (they loaded in float32, then went to bf16: twice
  the memory while loading, 26 GB on a 24 GB machine);
- the transparent decoder decodes one layer at a time, and skips the median
  of a single pass (MPS cannot sort 5-D tensors). Same results.
The rest (attention, group_norm, tag embeddings) is patched at run time by
rigkit/seethrough_local.py.

diff --git a/common/modules/layerdiffuse/vae.py b/common/modules/layerdiffuse/vae.py
